      "content": "To make the presentation mathematically certain, we should focus the formal report less on the 'feeling' of rest and more on demonstrable compliance metrics. We can restructure the justification around compliance checkpoints, emphasizing that every minute worked is logged and validated against regulatory maximums, leaving no ambiguity regarding legal adherence. Furthermore, instead of arguing the *quality* of the micro-breaks, we should highlight that the system *ensures* the mandated *duration* of these rest periods, making the claim objective and auditable.",
